; MCPd-Enable-Input - allow remote keyboard / mouse injection.
;
; Usage from a Shell on the target:
;     Execute SYS:System/MCPd/MCPd-Enable-Input
;
; Creates the sentinel file SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT. MCPd reads
; it ONCE at startup, so you must restart MCPd afterwards. That is
; deliberate: because the gate is only ever read at startup, no RPC
; method can turn input injection on at runtime. Turning it on
; requires filesystem access to this machine.
;
; The --enable-input command-line flag does the same thing, but does
; NOT survive a restart: MCPd-Watchdog relaunches MCPd with no
; arguments, and the S:Network-Startup line added by MCPd-Install has
; none either. Use this script for a persistent setting.
;
; To turn it back off: Execute SYS:System/MCPd/MCPd-Disable-Input

FailAt 21

If NOT EXISTS SYS:System/MCPd
  Echo "MCPd-Enable-Input: SYS:System/MCPd not found - run MCPd-Install first"
  Quit 20
EndIf

; NOTE: in AmigaDOS Echo, '*' is the ESCAPE character -- a literal
; asterisk must be written '**'. Using '=' for the rules avoids the
; whole problem and prints identically on every locale.
Echo ""
Echo "========================= WARNING ========================="
Echo "Enabling input injection lets ANY client that can reach this"
Echo "machine on TCP port 4322 type on the keyboard and move and"
Echo "click the mouse, as the logged-in user, in whatever window"
Echo "happens to be focused."
Echo ""
Echo "MCPd has NO authentication. The only thing protecting this"
Echo "machine is who can reach the port. Do not enable this on a"
Echo "target reachable from an untrusted network."
Echo "==========================================================="
Echo ""

Echo >SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT "input injection enabled by MCPd-Enable-Input"

If NOT EXISTS SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT
  Echo "MCPd-Enable-Input: FAILED to create the sentinel file"
  Quit 20
EndIf

Echo "MCPd-Enable-Input: sentinel created at SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT"
Echo ""
Echo "NOW RESTART MCPd - the gate is only read at startup."
Echo "  If running under the watchdog:  Break <its pid> C, it relaunches."
Echo "  Otherwise: Break the MCPd process and run it again."
Echo ""
; '******' renders as '***' -- see the escaping note above.
Echo "MCPd prints '****** INPUT INJECTION ENABLED ******' at startup when"
Echo "the gate is open. If you do not see that line, it is still off."
Quit 0
